{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/387408-is-there-a-book-that-details-what-happens-to-characters-of-cwod-by-end-of-gehenna","id":387408,"title":"Is there a book that details what happens to characters of CWOD by end of gehenna?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-31T08:14:54-08:00","id":387408,"title":"Is there a book that details what happens to characters of CWOD by end of gehenna?","content":"Yes, i am aware of the fiction novels as well the final gameplay books such as Time of Judgement - Vampire - Gehenna. But they cover a very very small part of the setting.<br /> <br /> For example, what happens to characters like Ur-Shulgi, who woke from torpor and was reshaping the assamite clan? What happened to him after Haqim woke up?<br /> <br /> What happened to infamous characters like Keminitri of the red list? Did the nictuku ever attack the nosferatu other than baba yaga? There were still tons of unresolved plot lines at the end of the Gehenna book. And lastly, what happens to all the thin bloods? Did they die like all the other vampires, or were turned into humans at last?<br /> <br /> The same goes for other settings like mage, werewolf, etc.<br /> <br /> Also is there a timeline of classic WOD that details which books are in chronological order? It is very frustrating reading a book like Gehenna and having it reference several events that occured in the past, but you have no idea what book to read to find the full story. For example, that book references Anatole's death...which book did that occur in? Its not mentioned anywhere i can find.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4880-question","name":"Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T08:24:36-08:00","id":387426,"title":"","content":"No, there is not. Time of Judgement brought a close to all of the OWoD lines. They give guidelines for after the Gehenna, Apocalypse, etc. But nothing more was written about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T09:36:59-08:00","id":387453,"title":"","content":"And in Gehenna and the rest they pretty coldly ignored most plot hooks they had been setting up for a long time so no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T09:37:14-08:00","id":387454,"title":"","content":"The thing is there is no one canon scenario in all the ToJ books, so what happens to specific characters depends upon the scenario and the Storyteller running. Plus there's no official post-ToJ material out there, leaving everything up to the individual groups.<br /> <br /> The only game-ending book that is different from the rest is <i>Ends of Empire</i>, Wrath: the Oblivion's final book. Unlike the rest it has only one scenario which allowed them to definitively the fates of many of the notable NPCs. In fact the back of the book has a list of all the major NPCs and what happened to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T12:51:51-08:00","id":387571,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, you could say yes, \u300aspoilers, ha ha ha\u300b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They all Die.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T01:00:48-08:00","id":388123,"title":"","content":"Of course there were unresolved plotlines... it's an RPG, the point of those plotlines is for you to resolve them in your games, if you care to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T03:47:00-08:00","id":388259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/387408-is-there-a-book-that-details-what-happens-to-characters-of-cwod-by-end-of-gehenna?p=387453#post387453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in Gehenna and the rest they pretty coldly ignored most plot hooks they had been setting up for a long time so no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all of them, Gehenna was the worst offender of that by a huge margin. There was a bit of everything in the others.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T03:51:17-08:00","id":388267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/387408-is-there-a-book-that-details-what-happens-to-characters-of-cwod-by-end-of-gehenna?p=388259#post388259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all of them, Gehenna was the worst offender of that by a huge margin. There was a bit of everything in the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage in particular (especially its main ToJ scenario) used lots of plot hooks from the gameline. I'd go so far as to say, if you weren't familiar with a bunch of stuff from Mage's history, that &quot;Judgement&quot; would seem pretty obscure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T03:58:37-08:00","id":388289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/387408-is-there-a-book-that-details-what-happens-to-characters-of-cwod-by-end-of-gehenna?p=388267#post388267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mage in particular (especially its main ToJ scenario) used lots of plot hooks from the gameline. I'd go so far as to say, if you weren't familiar with a bunch of stuff from Mage's history, that &quot;Judgement&quot; would seem pretty obscure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, true. The Apocalypse scenarios also used previously introduced plot hooks here and there. As I said, Gehenna was the real offender with that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T06:41:15-08:00","id":388378,"title":"","content":"Honestly I found that <i>Gehenna</i> at least had some interesting ideas despite not involving the metaplot as much as it could. And its still head and shoulders above the book, <i>Time of Judgement</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T09:25:33-08:00","id":388494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/387408-is-there-a-book-that-details-what-happens-to-characters-of-cwod-by-end-of-gehenna?p=388123#post388123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course there were unresolved plotlines... it's an RPG, the point of those plotlines is for you to resolve them in your games, if you care to.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could honestly question that with a lot of the CWOD metaplot. Or it often more than seemed like that. In some ways, the CWOD fluff was a really big sprawling epic story threaded throughout dozens of books by dozens of authors with the connections and resolutions set up as &quot;quests&quot; that need plot coupons from many sources to assemble. Oh, and are self-contradictory, changed, subject to internal misunderstanding and in jokes and suffering from lack of a continuity editor. <br /> <br /> And you couldn't really ignore it, either. Golden Rule aside, the fluff had huge impacts on the crunch. Ignore the metaplot and its effects and you would have to jury-rig in any new changes that you wanted to effect in your own games. <br /> <br /> That being the case, it's completely understandable that people want something close to 'official' resolution to the plots. That's been built in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T13:34:21-08:00","id":388833,"title":"","content":"I always treated the metaplot as a toolbox - take what you want, ignore what you don't, kitbash the whole to fit my needs. But I do often hear/read about folks who saw it all as canon, or wanted the sort of resolution that Ajax mentions.<br /> <br /> Where does everyone fall on this spectrum, between toolkit approach and canon adherence? What can one approach benefit from the other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T21:01:34-08:00","id":389393,"title":"","content":"It feels dissapointing because for example, the assassmite schism was a pretty major event, then it got mostly ignored at the end. A novel about what the antediluvians did after waking up and the clans' reaction to them would have made for great material...but the closest we got was one scenario in the time of judgement book that pretty much glossed it over in a few paragraphs. Would have looked a book about enoch and the second city as well, i cant even begin to imagine what it was like at that point in history.<br /> <br /> What about the other thing i mentioned though, the metaplot was developed through tons of books exactly, but what order do i read those in? See the beckett, etc example i mentioned.<br /> <br /> Edit : Oh by the way, can someone explain what happens in the novel, Judgement day for Mage? Unlike Gehenna and The Last Battle, there is no coherent storyline at all. Clearly, the characters with dual avatars were meant to do something...or at least thats what the rogue council felt...but what happens in the ending is not well explained...they die and merge into some godlike entity for the purpose of....what exactly? And what happens after everyone's souls are absorbed into the spheres?<br /> <br /> As for werewolf, if the wyrm was going to destroy gaia, why do gaia's spirits still have to be convinced to help the garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4880-question","user":"Question","date":". 02-02-2015, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4880-question","name":"Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T23:23:08-08:00","id":389473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Question</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/387408-is-there-a-book-that-details-what-happens-to-characters-of-cwod-by-end-of-gehenna?p=389393#post389393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for werewolf, if the wyrm was going to destroy gaia, why do gaia's spirits still have to be convinced to help the garou?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their track record, as well as, in some cases, the inability of some spirits to move on a rushed time scale. Also, the battles leading up the Apocalypse are about determining the shape of the world to come, not preventing an Earth-shattering kaboom or similarly dramatic event, so it might not be that a lot of spirits are immediately threatened with death, so they end up like climate change deniers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}